BlitzBench - BlitzTasks: Licensing

Copyright (c) 2026 Leon Freist / BlitzBench (https://blitzbench.de)

This repository is source-available and multi-licensed on a per-task basis:

1. Default license.
   Everything in this repository that is not covered by a per-task
   declaration (task-lib/, common/, catalog/, build tooling, and every task
   directory whose TASK.json declares the default) is licensed under the
   BlitzBench Source-Available License:
   LICENSES/LicenseRef-BlitzBench-Source-Available.txt
   In short: the source may be viewed and evaluated, but any other use,
   modification, or redistribution requires explicit written approval.

2. Per-task licenses.
   Each benchmark task directory (blitz-task_*/) declares its own license in
   its TASK.json under the top-level "license" key ({ "spdx", "file" }); the
   referenced text lives in LICENSES/. Some tasks are released under
   open-source licenses (e.g. GPL) because they link third-party libraries
   that require it (e.g. FFmpeg-based video tasks). See LICENSING.md for a
   generated per-task summary.

3. Shared framework code in per-task builds.
   Tasks link the shared framework code in task-lib/ and common/. For any
   task released under an open-source license, the copyright holder grants
   the right to build, link, and distribute the shared framework code as part
   of that task under the terms of that task's declared license.
   [NOTE: this clause is a working draft pending legal review.]

4. Third-party components.
   Third-party libraries remain under their own licenses. See
   THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md, third_party/, and each task's "libraries" metadata
   in its TASK.json.

Contact for permissions: Leon Freist <freist@blitzbench.de>
